# Keep the Docker build context small. The image build needs: the Go source
# (cmd/, pkg/, internal/, go.mod, go.sum); the embedded SPA sources
# (pkg/editorui/web, pkg/adminui/web — built by the node stages in the
# Dockerfile); examples/quickstart/schema.json (baked in); and
# docs/BACKEND_SPEC_LLM.md (//go:embed'd by backendspec.go). Everything below is
# excluded.

# VCS / CI
.git
.github

# Compiled binaries & build artifacts (the image builds its own binary)
/appximo
appximo_audit
*.pre_*
*.bundle
appximo-rollback/
coverage.out
*.out
*.test

# node_modules are regenerated by the Dockerfile's node stages (npm install),
# never copied from the host.
**/node_modules/

# The embedded SPA bundles are built by the Dockerfile's node stages and copied
# in with `COPY --from`, so the image is reproducible from a clean checkout and a
# dirty host can never leak stale JS. Exclude any host-built assets here.
pkg/editorui/web/build/
pkg/adminui/web/dist/

# Docs are not needed to compile the binary — EXCEPT the files the binary
# //go:embed's (the sources of `appximo backend-spec`, `frontend-spec`,
# `backoffice-spec`, `quickstart` and `prompt`). Excluding docs/ WITHOUT
# re-including one of them breaks the image build:
#   pattern docs/FRONTEND_SPEC_LLM.md: no matching files found
# That has now happened FOUR times — each time a new embedded doc landed and
# nothing built the image before the push. The list below is no longer
# maintained by memory: TestDockerignoreKeepsEmbeddedDocs (dockerignore_test.go)
# fails the unit lane whenever a //go:embed docs/... path is missing here.
*.md
!README.md
context-docs/
benchmarks/
docs/
!docs/BACKEND_SPEC_LLM.md
!docs/FRONTEND_SPEC_LLM.md
!docs/BACKOFFICE_SPEC_LLM.md
!docs/LIFECYCLE_SPEC_LLM.md
!docs/MASTER_PROMPT.md
!docs/INSTALL_PROMPT.md

# Local env / secrets (never send to the build)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
